  "description": "DEP-03 re-arm on one armer's fork: a later DisputeArmed must repeat the commitment_hash and must declare replacement collateral; a fresh pledge (collateral after collateral) is allowed. Shared by cl-deposits (inspect/rotation-test.lisp) and deposits-rust (deposits-core ledger tests). DEP-06 Phase 4 (strict-lottery-v8, provisional): an arm carrying rearm_round (TLV 366) above the fork's last arm round starts that round with a fresh commitment, from an armed or a yielded fork; a lower round is refused; within a round the rules above hold. Under strict-lottery-v8 (acquire-on-confirm, ruled 2026-11-10) a fork that armed and then published a DisputeAcquire takes a later round's arm: a claim that confirmed would have spent the lottery output, so a later round means it never landed (cases with acquire_between and ruleset).",
